WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.510
A long French article
about young volunteers.

2
00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:06.290
Your summary gets only a few short lines.

3
00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.820
In it, «Léa» works in a community grocery.

4
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.860
At first, she just wanted a better CV.

5
00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.980
Does that belong in your few lines?

6
00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.630
And if it does, in whose words?

7
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:21.810
So how do you shrink a French
article into a short summary,

8
00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.540
without simply copying its sentences?

9
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.070
In this mission, you'll
feed a source text through

10
00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.810
the summary funnel in Mission D1.

11
00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:34.140
Then you'll take the «Léa»
text apart in Mission D3,

12
00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.810
and see where every sentence ends up.

13
00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:39.210
Your mission: find out what stays,

14
00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:42.270
what goes, and how to
write it without copying.
